                    <h3>Specific Services</h3>
                    <p class="text-justify">
                        Our team at <a href="/"><strong>© Opportunity Painting And Renovation Services Inc.</strong></a> offers a range of specialized services tailored to meet your kitchen cabinet needs:
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong><a href="/service-kitchen-cabinet-refinishing.html">Cabinet Transformation:</a></strong> Our expert painters can completely transform the look of your cabinets, updating them with fresh paint and modern hardware.</li>
                        <li><strong><a href="/service-kitchen-cabinet-refinishing.html">Restoration and Painting:</a></strong> We restore the beauty of your cabinets with meticulous attention to detail, providing custom painting services to suit your preferences.</li>
                        <li><strong><a href="/service-kitchen-cabinet-refinishing.html">High-Quality Finishes:</a></strong> Utilizing top-quality paints and stains, we ensure durable and long-lasting finishes that enhance the overall appearance of your kitchen.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h3>Benefits of Our Services</h3>
                    <p class="text-justify">
                        When you choose <a href="/"><strong>© Opportunity Painting And Renovation Services Inc.</strong></a> for your kitchen cabinet painting needs, you benefit from:
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Professional consultation and personalized service</li>
                        <li>Economical alternatives to cabinet replacement</li>
                        <li>Durable finishes that stand the test of time</li>
                        <li>Skilled craftsmanship and attention to detail</li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="mt-5 mb-4">
                        <span class="section-title">FACTORY-SMOOTH REGIMEN</span>
                        <h2 class="display-6 mt-1 mb-3">Our 7-Step Factory-Smooth Refinishing Process</h2>
                        <p class="text-justify mb-4">
                            The difference between DIY cabinet painting and professional refinishing is our 7-step industrial finishing regimen:
                        </p>

                        <div class="editorial-process">
                            <div class="editorial-step">
                                <h3 class="editorial-step-title"><span class="step-num-accent">01.</span> Hardware Removal &amp; Labeling</h3>
                                <p class="text-justify">
                                    Removing all cabinet doors, drawer fronts, and hardware. Every component is indexed to ensure exact realignment during reinstallation.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="editorial-step">
                                <h3 class="editorial-step-title"><span class="step-num-accent">02.</span> Deep Chemical Degreasing</h3>
                                <p class="text-justify">
                                    Cleaning surfaces with specialized degreasers to remove decades of airborne cooking oils, grease, and residue that impede coating adhesion.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="editorial-step">
                                <h3 class="editorial-step-title"><span class="step-num-accent">03.</span> Mechanical Sanding &amp; Profiling</h3>
                                <p class="text-justify">
                                    Dustless orbital sanding of all woodwork to remove failing varnish and profile the wood grain for maximum mechanical bond.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="editorial-step">
                                <h3 class="editorial-step-title"><span class="step-num-accent">04.</span> High-Adhesion Stain-Blocking Primer</h3>
                                <p class="text-justify">
                                    Applying industrial shellac or high-bonding bonding primer that locks in tannins, seals open wood pores, and establishes a rock-solid foundation.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="editorial-step">
                                <h3 class="editorial-step-title"><span class="step-num-accent">05.</span> Inter-Coat Sanding &amp; Imperfection Fill</h3>
                                <p class="text-justify">
                                    Hand-sanding between coats and filling wood voids or dings with high-durability timber filler for a mirror-smooth tactile surface.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="editorial-step">
                                <h3 class="editorial-step-title"><span class="step-num-accent">06.</span> Airless Spray Application of Enamel</h3>
                                <p class="text-justify">
                                    Spraying multiple coats of premium cabinet-grade polyurethane enamel (such as Benjamin Moore Advance or Renner wood coatings) for an enduring factory finish.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="editorial-step">
                                <h3 class="editorial-step-title"><span class="step-num-accent">07.</span> Reassembly &amp; Hardware Upgrade</h3>
                                <p class="text-justify">
                                    Reinstalling doors and drawers with precision laser alignment, installing new handles or pulls, and upgrading hinges to soft-close if requested.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
