                        <h2 class="display-6 mt-1 mb-2">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faq-accordion">
                        <details>
                            <summary>What is the difference between painting cabinets and cabinet refinishing?</summary>
                            <p class="faq-answer">
                                Regular house painting often relies on brush or roller application, which can leave brush strokes and chip easily. Our cabinet refinishing uses industrial spray systems with high-solids polyurethane/enamel coatings that create an ultra-durable, factory-smooth finish identical to brand-new high-end cabinets.
                            </p>
                        </details>
                        <details>
                            <summary>How much money does cabinet refinishing save compared to replacing cabinets?</summary>
                            <p class="faq-answer">
                                Refinishing existing solid wood cabinet boxes and doors typically saves 60% to 75% compared to custom cabinet replacement, while avoiding weeks of kitchen downtime and countertop removal.
                            </p>
                        </details>
                        <details>
                            <summary>How long does cabinet spray refinishing last?</summary>
                            <p class="faq-answer">
                                With proper care, our multi-coat catalyzed urethane finishes last 10 to 15+ years. They resist cooking grease, moisture, fingerprints, and household cleaning chemicals without chipping or peeling.
                            </p>
                        </details>
                        <details>
                            <summary>Do you spray cabinet doors on-site in my home?</summary>
                            <p class="faq-answer">
                                No. We carefully remove all cabinet doors and drawer fronts, label each piece, and transport them to our controlled spray facility for degreasing, sanding, priming, and spray finishing. Only the exterior cabinet frame boxes are prepped and sprayed in your home inside a fully sealed plastic spray containment booth.
                            </p>
                        </details>
                        <details>
                            <summary>Can my cabinets be refinished, or do they need to be replaced?</summary>
                            <p class="faq-answer">
                                If the cabinet boxes are solid, refinishing can give them a new look without the cost and disruption of replacement. We will look at their condition and tell you honestly which option makes sense.
                            </p>
                        </details>
                        <details>
                            <summary>Do you offer cabinet refinishing in Framingham and nearby towns?</summary>
                            <p class="faq-answer">
                                Yes. We are based in Holliston and also serve Framingham, Hopkinton, Milford, Medway, Ashland, Sherborn, Millis, Dover, Medfield, Natick and Franklin. If you are not sure we cover your address, call us at (508) 215-9441.
                            </p>
                        </details>
                        <details>
                            <summary>Do you offer free estimates and a warranty?</summary>
                            <p class="faq-answer">
                                Yes. We visit the property, talk through the work and give you a detailed quote at no cost. We also offer a written workmanship warranty, and the terms are detailed in your contract.
                            </p>
                        </details>
